– Mandate of the Task Force on the Mindanao River Basin Rehabilitation and Development. –
The Task Force shall:
a. Coordinate the formulation and implementation of the MRB Relief, Rehabilitation and Long-Term
Development Plan;
b. Integrate flood control efforts in the areas of ARMM and Region XII that were flooded by Typhoons Frank
c. Ensure that public funds for the rehabilitation and development of the MRB shall be spend judiciously and
effectively through efficient prioritization of programs and consistent monitoring of projects;
d. Serve as clearing house for all proposals related to the development of the MRB;
e. Upon consultation and evaluation, approve appropriate requests;
f. Notify the Department of Budget and Management (DBM) of its approval as bass for the release of funds.

Functions. – The Task Force shall have the following powers and functions:
a. Generate proposals from implementing agencies for the rehabilitation and development of the MRB;
b. Identify and package the rehabilitation and long-term interventions for the MRB affected areas;
c. Decide on important interventions that need to be immediately implemented or acted upon;
d. Spearhead and coordinate all courses of action to ensure cohesiveness in objectives and coordinated action
to improve the implementation of flood control repair, construction works and other rehabilitation and
development initiatives in the MRB;

e. Work with concerned national agencies (such as the Department of Public Works and Highways (DPWH))
and the Autonomous Region of Muslim Mindanao (ARMM) for the important interventions that need to be
implemented for flood control and other projects pertaining to the rehabilitation and development of the MRB;
f. Work with the Regional Development Councils (RDCs) of the ARMM and Region XII on common or
overlapping project activities related to flood control and other rehabilitation and development initiatives in
g. Negotiate, apply for, receive and accept grants and donations of funds needed for the relief, rehabilitation
and development of the areas affected by the disaster;
h. Conduct resource mobilization activities, such as, but not limited to:
(i) Enjoining the concerned local government units to pass ordinances appropriating local resources for
identified interventions;
(ii) Requesting funds from the National Disaster Coordinating Council;
(iii) Ensuring inclusion of rehabilitation plans of Regional Line Agencies in their annual operational plans or
realign funds, if necessary;
(iv) Conducting special Official Development Assistance pledging sessions to be spearheaded by the RDCs
and the Regional Disaster Coordinating Councils of Region XII and ARMM;
(v) Enjoining Congress to include a special purpose fund for rehabilitation and development in the General
Appropriations Act of Fiscal Year 2009 and beyond.
i. Regularly monitor the status of programs, projects and activities related to Cotabato flood control in the
areas flooded by Typhoons Frank and Cosme, as well as the other rehabilitation and development projects in
the MRB to ensure their prompt and efficient execution;
j. Recommend action to improve the implementation of flood control repair and other related rehabilitation
and development initiatives in the MRB;
k. Coordinate and consult with concerned national and local government officials, both elective and
appointive, as well as accredited non-governmental organizations in the prosecution of programs and projects;
l. Formulate policies, plans and programs of the MRB with regard to flood control funds or funds for similar
purpose that may be allocated for the MRB flood conrol and rehabilitation and development;
m. Mobilize the assistance and support of any government agency or instrumentality as well as civil society
and the donor community to address identified gaps and requirements in the MRB; and
n. Perform other activities pursuant to the orders of the President.

Powers and Functions of the Executive Director of the Secretariat. – The Secretariat of the Task
Force shall have the following powers and functions:
a. Administer and manage the day-to-day affairs and operations of the Task Force;
b. Coordinate the activities of agencies and instrumentalities in the implementation of projects;
c. Coordiante and liaise with accredited non-government organizations, international agencies and other
groups or individuals involved in flood control;
d. Initiate the conduct of studies on flood control and related environmental and hydrological studies to
minimize the adverse effects to lives, properties and livelihood of residents in the MRB that may be caused by
similar floods;
e. Work with the DPWH and other concerned agencies on engineering and other related plans for the MRB;
f. Monitor the implementation of projects and programs in connection with the rehabilitation and development

g. Report to the Task Force, which shall meet at least monthly, on the status, situation and developments
concerning projects and programs;
h. Act as the Head of the Secretariat of the Task Force; and
i. Perform such other functions as may be assigned by the President of the Philippines.
